{
  "name": "sturgeon",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/sturgeons.py): a sturgeon (Atlantic / European, Acipenser sturio), 1.8 m -- slender, the snout long, narrow, flattened and pointed with FOUR round BARBELS in a row across its underside, the small toothless mouth UNDER the head behind them; FIVE ROWS OF BONY SCUTES, pale and sharply keeled (one down the back, one along each flank, one along each side of the belly); a small eye; the dorsal fin far back over the anal, broad low pectorals, pelvics before the anal; the SHARK-LIKE (heterocercal) tail, the body running up into its long upper lobe; olive-brown-grey above, a cream belly. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A slow SWIMMER near the bottom (the fish's plumbing).",
